<title>USA: ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in 199.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in 199.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 487 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>	 The world's 20 busiest cargo airports last year, with the</p>
<p>volume they handled, their 1995 ranking and the percentage change on 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>		   AIRPORT			1996 TONNAGE	  PCT</p>
<p>CHANGE FROM 1995</p>
<p>1  (1)  Memphis		     1,932,607 tonnes	 (up 12.9 pct)</p>
<p>2  (3)  Los Angeles		 1,719,502 tonnes	 (up  7.7)</p>
<p>3  (4)  Miami			 1,709,935 tonnes	 (up  7.9)</p>
<p>4  (5)  New York		    1,631,073 tonnes	 (up  2.9)</p>
<p>5  (2)  Tokyo-Narita		1,625,840 tonnes	(down 2.5)</p>
<p>6  (6)  Hong Kong		   1,590,772 tonnes	 (up  7.1)</p>
<p>7  (7)  Frankfurt		   1,497,354 tonnes	 (up  2.5)</p>
<p>8  (8)  Louisville		  1,368,701 tonnes	 (up  1.3)</p>
<p>9 (10)  Seoul			 1,361,510 tonnes	 (up 12.0)</p>
<p>10 (16)  Anchorage		   1,269,283 tonnes	(up 29.7)</p>
<p>11  (9)  Chicago		     1,254,789 tonnes	(up  1.5)</p>
<p>12 (12)  Singapore		   1,211,411 tonnes	(up  7.7)</p>
<p>13 (11)  London Heathrow	   1,140,768 tonnes	(up  1.3)</p>
<p>14 (13)  Amsterdam		   1,124,649 tonnes	(up 10.3)</p>
<p>15 (15)  Paris-CDG		     978,722 tonnes	(up  5.3)</p>
<p>16 (14)  New York Newark	     957,782 tonnes	(up  1.6)</p>
<p>17 (18)  Atlanta			 800,378 tonnes	(up  3.9)</p>
<p>18 (19)  Taipei			  796,155 tonnes	(up  5.8)</p>
<p>19 (17)  Dallas Fort Worth	   785,694 tonnes	(up  1.1)</p>
<p>20  (-)  Dayton			  727,165 tonnes	(up 14.9) - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
